# versions.env — every pinned version in this repository lives here. Nothing else pins.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line, NO command substitution and no logic.
# Loaded with `set -a; . versions.env; set +a` by lib/common.sh's devenv_version_env,
# so every key is exported into every module.
#
# =============================================================================
# THE TAG RULE  (MUST-FIX C7 / correctness C9) — one rule, applied everywhere.
#
#   Every *_VERSION below is the UPSTREAM RELEASE TAG, VERBATIM, in that project's
#   own form. Some projects prefix their tags with `v` and some do not; both forms
#   appear here on purpose and neither is a mistake:
#       DIVE_VERSION=v0.13.1        dive's tag IS v0.13.1  (0.13.1 -> 404)
#       DELTA_VERSION=0.18.2        dandavison/delta tags carry no `v`
#       FASTFETCH_VERSION=2.68.1    fastfetch tags carry no `v`
#
#   lib/net.sh derives both spellings from the pin, so an asset pattern never has to
#   know which convention a project uses:
#       {tag}      the pin, verbatim                    v0.13.1   kustomize/v5.8.1
#       {version}  {tag} minus any component prefix
#                  and minus one leading `v`            0.13.1    5.8.1
#   Download URLs use {tag}; asset FILENAMES usually use {version}.
#   Never "normalise" a pin to make it look like its neighbours.
#
# SENTINEL VALUES
#   latest   resolved at install time from the releases/latest 302 Location header
#            (no api.github.com, so no 60-requests-per-hour rate limit), asserted to
#            be a real /releases/tag/ URL, and cached for 6 h.
#   apt      not pinned here at all: the version comes from the vendor's apt repo.
#   auto     only for K8S_MINOR: enables the three-tier cluster/stable.txt probe.
#
#   Pins that are currently `latest`, i.e. that float:
#       MISE_VERSION  GO_TOOL_GOIMPORTS  OPENCODE_VERSION  CLAUDE_CODE_CHANNEL(stable)
#       TMUX_VERSION (only on the from-source path)  PLAYWRIGHT_VERSION (an npm spec)
#   Everything else is a fixed tag.
#
# NAMING (idempotency F23). This whole file is exported into every child process, so
# a key must never collide with a variable a tool itself reads. Use one of these
# suffixes and nothing else:
#       _VERSION  _REF  _MINOR  _CHANNEL  _MANAGER  _DIR_DEFAULT  _KEY_SHA256
#   plus the explicit INSTALL_* / *_TOOL_* feature gates at the bottom.
#
# `# owner:` names the module that installs the thing (SPEC 5.5 + SPEC-ADDENDUM 5.1).
# Every pin here has exactly one owner — MUST-FIX P3, no orphans. Things with no
# owner are listed, unpinned, in the final section.
#
# `tools/bump-versions.sh` resolves each `# renovate: datasource=github-releases
# depName=<owner>/<repo>` line through the 302 header (releases.atom as a second
# fallback), rewrites ONE key at a time with sed so comments and deliberate pins
# survive, and skips any pin whose value is `apt` or `latest`.
#
# ANNOTATIONS. Every pin below now carries either a `# renovate:` line or a
# `# no-datasource:` line saying why it cannot have one, ON THE LINE DIRECTLY
# ABOVE THE PIN — both Renovate and bump-versions.sh require that adjacency, so
# nothing may be inserted between the two. A trailing `# …` note after depName is
# safe: both parsers stop the depName capture at the first space.
#
# THREE PLACES WHERE THE 302 HEADER IS NOT THE ANSWER. bump-versions.sh has no
# --tag-filter and no `# pin-policy: manual` check of its own; it used to skip the
# manual pins only as a side effect of the pin-policy comment sitting between the
# annotation and the pin, and that comment is no longer the adjacent line.
#   pin-policy: manual   HELM_VERSION and VIRTCTL_VERSION are now visible to
#                        `make bump-write`. helm/helm's latest is already v4.x, so
#                        teach the script the pin-policy rule before using --write.
#   KUSTOMIZE_VERSION    releases/latest is `kustomize/v5.8.1`; this pin holds the
#                        bare `v5.8.1` and modules/35 re-adds the prefix. The
#                        annotation's extractVersion= tells Renovate the same thing.
#   KOR_VERSION          releases/latest is the Helm-CHART tag (kor-0.x), not the CLI.
# =============================================================================

## ---------- language runtimes ----------
# owner: lang-go
# renovate: datasource=golang-version depName=go
GO_VERSION=1.27.1
# owner: lang-node
# renovate: datasource=node-version depName=node
NODE_VERSION=24
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=nvm-sh/nvm
NVM_VERSION=v0.40.7
# MUST match ~/.bashrc.d/20-lang.sh. $HOME expands because the file is sourced.
# no-datasource: a filesystem path, not a version.
NVM_DIR_DEFAULT=$HOME/.config/nvm
# no-datasource: a mode switch (nvm|mise), not a version.
NODE_MANAGER=nvm
# owner: lang-python — foundational: installed before any Python CLI
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=astral-sh/uv
UV_VERSION=0.12.12
# owner: lang-node — only consulted when NODE_MANAGER=mise (opt-in, K7)
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=jdx/mise
MISE_VERSION=latest
# owner: lang-rust — rustup has no meaningful pin; the toolchain self-manages
# no-datasource: a rustup CHANNEL name; rustup resolves and self-manages the toolchain.
RUST_TOOLCHAIN=stable

## ---------- kubernetes core ----------
# owner: kubernetes (module 35) unless noted
# pin-policy: manual — match the fleet's k3s minor, +/-1 skew max. `auto` probes.
# kubernetes/kubernetes releases would resolve v1.34.x, which is not a valid stream path.
# no-datasource: a MINOR STREAM for the pkgs.k8s.io apt URL, not a release tag.
K8S_MINOR=v1.34
# pin-policy: manual — Helm v4.x exists; a bootstrap script must not jump majors.
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=helm/helm  # 3.x deliberately: upstream latest is already v4.x
HELM_VERSION=v3.22.0
# owner: k8s-plugins
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=kubernetes-sigs/krew
KREW_VERSION=v0.5.0
# k9s trap: the TARBALL is k9s_Linux_<arch>.tar.gz (capital L), the DEB is
# k9s_linux_<arch>.deb (lower case). Both exist for every release.
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=derailed/k9s
K9S_VERSION=v0.51.0
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=kubecolor/kubecolor  # the project moved here from hidetatz/kubecolor
KUBECOLOR_VERSION=v0.7.1
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=k3d-io/k3d
K3D_VERSION=v5.9.0
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=kubernetes-sigs/kind
KIND_VERSION=v0.33.0
# tags are component-prefixed (kustomize/v5.8.1) -> --tag-filter '^kustomize/'
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=kubernetes-sigs/kustomize extractVersion=^kustomize/(?<version>.+)$  # monorepo: real tags are kustomize/vX.Y.Z, this pin holds the bare vX.Y.Z
KUSTOMIZE_VERSION=v5.8.1
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=yannh/kubeconform
KUBECONFORM_VERSION=v0.8.0
# the standalone CLI, NOT the krew `cilium` plugin. Both are installed (K10).
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=cilium/cilium-cli  # the CLI's own repo, NOT cilium/cilium (the CNI)
CILIUM_CLI_VERSION=v0.20.0
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=cilium/hubble  # the CLI's own repo; it tracks cilium/cilium loosely and SKIPS patch numbers
# tag-filter: v1.18.*  # the hubble CLI tracks the CNI minor: bump this with cilium, not ahead of it
HUBBLE_VERSION=v1.18.3
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=argoproj/argo-cd
ARGOCD_VERSION=v3.5.2
# pin-policy: manual — MUST match the cluster's KubeVirt version. Installed
# ALONGSIDE krew `virt` (K11): config/k9s/plugins/63-kubevirt.yaml calls `virtctl`.
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=kubevirt/kubevirt  # virtctl ships out of the kubevirt monorepo release
VIRTCTL_VERSION=v1.9.0
# Azure's kubelogin. A DIFFERENT project from krew `oidc-login` (int128/kubelogin).
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=Azure/kubelogin  # AZURE's; NOT int128/kubelogin, which krew installs as oidc-login
KUBELOGIN_VERSION=v0.2.19
# Crunchy PGO's official CLI — not in the krew index.
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=CrunchyData/postgres-operator-client  # not postgres-operator (the operator itself)
KUBECTL_PGO_VERSION=v0.5.3
# the repo was RENAMED vmware-tanzu/velero -> velero-io/velero; `releases/latest`
# redirects across the rename, which is why lib/net.sh follows redirects (C6).
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=velero-io/velero  # renamed from vmware-tanzu/velero
VELERO_VERSION=v1.18.2
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=kubernetes-sigs/cri-tools  # crictl has no repo of its own; it lives in cri-tools
CRICTL_VERSION=v1.37.0
# tag IS v0.13.1; the ASSET drops the v: dive_0.13.1_linux_amd64.deb (verified).
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=wagoodman/dive
DIVE_VERSION=v0.13.1
# mikefarah's yq v4, installed to /usr/local/bin. The distro `yq` is kislyuk's
# Python jq-wrapper and is NOT a replacement (K29). It is reported, never removed.
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=mikefarah/yq  # v4; NOT kislyuk/yq, which is the distro package of the same name
YQ_VERSION=v4.53.6

## ---------- kubernetes, opt-in (INSTALL_K8S_OPT=1) ----------
# owner: kubernetes — off by default; `full` does NOT turn these on.
# NOT `latest`: yonahd/kor's releases/latest points at the Helm-CHART tag.
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=yonahd/kor  # releases/latest is the HELM-CHART tag (kor-0.x); the CLI tags are vX.Y.Z
# tag-filter: v*
KOR_VERSION=v0.6.9
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=stackrox/kube-linter
KUBE_LINTER_VERSION=v0.8.3
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=aquasecurity/kube-bench
KUBE_BENCH_VERSION=v0.16.0
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=containerd/nerdctl
NERDCTL_VERSION=v2.1.6
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=bitnami-labs/sealed-secrets  # kubeseal is an asset of the sealed-secrets release; the repo now redirects to bitnami/sealed-secrets (verified)
KUBESEAL_VERSION=v0.33.1

## ---------- helm plugins (owner: k8s-plugins) ----------
# Registered names, which are what `helm plugin list` shows and what the guard
# matches: diff, schema, unittest, secrets, helm-git.
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=databus23/helm-diff
HELM_DIFF_VERSION=v3.15.12
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=helm-unittest/helm-unittest  # moved here from quintush/helm-unittest
HELM_UNITTEST_VERSION=v1.1.2
# losisin/helm-values-schema-json, registered as `schema`. REPLACES the archived
# karuppiah7890/helm-schema-gen (last push 2021-07-08), which is reported with the
# uninstall command but NEVER uninstalled for the user (K28).
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=losisin/helm-values-schema-json  # registered as `schema`; NOT karuppiah7890/helm-schema-gen
HELM_SCHEMA_VERSION=v2.6.0
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=jkroepke/helm-secrets  # moved here from zendesk/helm-secrets
HELM_SECRETS_VERSION=v4.7.0

## ---------- helm tooling (owner: k8s-plugins) ----------
# NOT a helm plugin: a standalone binary that renders chart READMEs. It was in the
# old scripts/tools.sh and must not be dropped silently (completeness F5).
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=norwoodj/helm-docs
HELM_DOCS_VERSION=v1.14.2

## ---------- iac / security (owner: iac) ----------
# from the HashiCorp apt repo; `apt` means "do not pin, the repo decides".
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=hashicorp/terraform  # value stays `apt` (the HashiCorp repo decides); upstream recorded so a reader can see it
TERRAFORM_VERSION=apt
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=terraform-linters/tflint
TFLINT_VERSION=v0.64.0
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=terraform-docs/terraform-docs
TERRAFORM_DOCS_VERSION=v0.24.0
# owner: kubernetes — from the trivy apt repo (suite `generic`, identical on both distros)
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=aquasecurity/trivy  # value stays `apt` (the trivy repo decides); upstream recorded so a reader can see it
TRIVY_VERSION=apt
# asset openbao_{version}_linux_{arch_dpkg}.deb, dpkg package `openbao`,
# BINARY `bao` (MUST-FIX C7 — bao_*.deb is a 404 and PKG=bao never matches dpkg).
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=openbao/openbao  # the LinuxFoundation fork of hashicorp/vault; not interchangeable
OPENBAO_VERSION=v2.6.2

## ---------- general CLI ----------
# owner: editors
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=neovim/neovim
NEOVIM_VERSION=v0.12.5
# owner: editors — read ONLY on the TMUX_FROM_SOURCE=1 path (apt tmux otherwise),
# which is why it floats: someone who asks to build tmux wants the current one.
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=tmux/tmux
TMUX_VERSION=latest
# owner: shell — absent from bookworm and jammy entirely, so always the tarball (K19)
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=eza-community/eza  # the maintained fork of the abandoned ogham/exa
EZA_VERSION=v0.23.5
# owner: shell
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=sxyazi/yazi
YAZI_VERSION=v26.9.1
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=fastfetch-cli/fastfetch  # tags carry no leading v (see THE TAG RULE)
FASTFETCH_VERSION=2.68.1
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=starship/starship
STARSHIP_VERSION=v1.26.0
# release-binary fallback only; the repo was RENAMED dbrgn -> tealdeer-rs (C6)
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=tealdeer-rs/tealdeer  # renamed from dbrgn/tealdeer; the Rust tldr client
TEALDEER_VERSION=v1.8.1
# apt_or_release fallbacks. The MINIMUM apt candidate that is good enough is passed
# to apt_or_release at the call site, not stored here: fzf 0.48.0 (the `fzf --bash`
# cutover), zoxide 0.9.0, git-delta 0.16.0.
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=dandavison/delta  # tags carry no leading v (see THE TAG RULE)
DELTA_VERSION=0.18.2
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=ajeetdsouza/zoxide
ZOXIDE_VERSION=v0.10.0
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=junegunn/fzf
FZF_VERSION=v0.74.3
# owner: shell — NerdFontsSymbolsOnly asset, and only on a box that is neither WSL
# nor headless (SPEC-ADDENDUM 5.2: glyphs are drawn by the terminal's own host).
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=ryanoasis/nerd-fonts
NERD_FONT_VERSION=v3.4.0
# owner: kubernetes
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=fullstorydev/grpcurl
GRPCURL_VERSION=v1.9.4
# owner: repo-dev
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=golangci/golangci-lint
GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION=v2.13.2
# owner: cloud — released on GITLAB.COM (gitlab-org/cli), not GitHub: the GitHub
# releases feed for this project is empty.
# renovate: datasource=gitlab-releases depName=gitlab-org/cli  # gitlab.com, not GitHub — tools/bump-versions.sh (github-releases only) skips this by design
GLAB_VERSION=v1.117.0

## ---------- go-installed tools: `go install MODULE@VERSION` ----------
# owner: lang-go, except where noted
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=google/go-containerregistry  # module github.com/google/go-containerregistry; tag == module version
GO_TOOL_CRANE=v0.20.6
# golang.org/x/tools — no release tags worth pinning; safe to float
# renovate: datasource=go depName=golang.org/x/tools  # no product release tags — the `go` datasource is the only source for this module
GO_TOOL_GOIMPORTS=latest
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=swaggo/swag  # releases/latest can be a v2 -rc tag; this pin deliberately holds the v1 line
GO_TOOL_SWAG=v1.16.4
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=a-h/templ
GO_TOOL_TEMPL=v0.3.906
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=Melkeydev/go-blueprint
GO_TOOL_GO_BLUEPRINT=v0.10.9
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=dundee/gdu  # module path carries the /v5 major suffix; the tag does not
GO_TOOL_GDU=v5.31.0
# owner: cloud
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=hetznercloud/cli  # hcloud is built from hetznercloud/cli, not hetznercloud/hcloud-go
GO_TOOL_HCLOUD=v1.53.0
# owner: repo-dev
# renovate: datasource=go depName=mvdan.cc/sh/v3  # vanity module path for github.com/mvdan/sh
GO_TOOL_SHFMT=v3.10.0

## ---------- headless browser automation ----------
# owner: headless-browser — in no profile; `devenv --only headless-browser`.
# This is an npm SPEC, not a release tag: the module hands it to
# `npx playwright@<spec> install-deps` and never maintains a package list of its
# own. `latest` is the vendor's own default; pin it when a project needs a fixed
# Playwright, because the dependency set changes between majors.
# renovate: datasource=npm depName=playwright  # an npm SPEC handed to `npx playwright@<spec>`, not a GitHub tag
PLAYWRIGHT_VERSION=latest

## ---------- ai agents ----------
# owner: ai
# Claude Code is a BASE install (user requirement #5): the NATIVE installer, not
# npm. `npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code` is the WRONG path — the live box
# has ~/.local/bin/claude -> ~/.local/share/claude/versions/<v>. Install if absent
# and then leave it alone: Claude Code self-updates, and this repo never runs
# `claude update` (correctness C20).
# Claude Code self-updates and this repo never pins it; the npm package is the wrong path (C20).
# no-datasource: an installer CHANNEL (stable|latest|X.Y.Z), not a version.
CLAUDE_CODE_CHANNEL=stable
# opt-in `ai` profile only. The vendor installer redirects to anomalyco/opencode;
# do not hardcode the old URL.
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=anomalyco/opencode  # sst/opencode redirects here; the module still uses the vendor installer URL
OPENCODE_VERSION=latest
# opt-in `ai` profile only (was GO_TOOL_CRUSH; it is an AI agent, not Go tooling).
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=charmbracelet/crush
CRUSH_VERSION=v0.93.1
# owner: lang-python — GitHub Spec Kit, installed with `uv tool install --from git+...`
# renovate: datasource=github-releases depName=github/spec-kit  # key ends in _REF, so bump-versions.sh (which matches *_VERSION=) never sees it
SPEC_KIT_REF=v1.0.6

## ---------- external config repos (git refs, not versions) ----------
# owner: editors — cloned and SYMLINKED, never curl-piped, and never updated over a
# dirty worktree.
# Renovate's git-refs datasource would replace a branch with a commit sha, which is not what a
# tracked branch is, so all three refs below are deliberately left unwatched.
# no-datasource: a BRANCH name (github.com/Ujstor/tmux-config), not a version.
TMUX_CONFIG_REF=master
# no-datasource: a branch name (github.com/Ujstor/nvim-config), as above.
NVIM_CONFIG_REF=master
# owner: shell — DETECT AND REPORT ONLY by default (idempotency F22): mybash owns
# ~/.bashrc on the live box and re-running its setup.sh is a data-loss event. This
# ref is used only when DEVENV_INSTALL_MYBASH=1 asks for a clone.
# no-datasource: a branch name (github.com/Ujstor/mybash), as above.
MYBASH_REF=main

## ---------- apt signing keys: optional digest pinning ----------
# idempotency F15. An apt signing key is root-equivalent trust for everything that
# repo will ever serve, and "it looks like a PGP block" is the only other check.
# Leave a value EMPTY to accept whatever the vendor serves (still validated as a
# real OpenPGP key). Set it to the sha256 of the fetched key FILE to pin it:
# lib/repo.sh then re-fetches on a mismatch instead of trusting the local copy
# forever. Rotate deliberately by updating the digest here.
# All six are sha256 digests of KEY FILES, not versions: rotating one is a deliberate trust
# decision (see above), so no datasource is wired up for any of them.
# no-datasource: sha256 digest of the Docker apt signing key file, not a version.
DOCKER_KEY_SHA256=
# no-datasource: sha256 digest of the HashiCorp apt signing key file, not a version.
HASHICORP_KEY_SHA256=
# no-datasource: sha256 digest of the pkgs.k8s.io apt signing key file, not a version.
KUBERNETES_KEY_SHA256=
# no-datasource: sha256 digest of the GitHub CLI apt signing key file, not a version.
GITHUB_CLI_KEY_SHA256=
# no-datasource: sha256 digest of the Azure CLI apt signing key file, not a version.
AZURE_CLI_KEY_SHA256=
# no-datasource: sha256 digest of the Trivy apt signing key file, not a version.
TRIVY_KEY_SHA256=

## ---------- feature gates ----------
# Not versions, but they belong to the same single source of truth. Every one of
# them is off by default; `full` sets the first three.
# Every switch below is a boolean, so none of them can carry a datasource.
# no-datasource: a boolean gate (extra krew plugins), not a version.
KREW_EXTRAS=0
# no-datasource: a boolean gate (packer), not a version.
INSTALL_PACKER=0
# no-datasource: a boolean gate (extra CLI tools), not a version.
INSTALL_EXTRAS=0
# kor / kube-linter / kube-bench / nerdctl / kubeseal, pinned above.
# no-datasource: a boolean gate (the opt-in k8s set), not a version.
INSTALL_K8S_OPT=0
# Homebrew: audit and migration map by default. Refuses below glibc 2.39 (K9).
# no-datasource: a boolean gate (homebrew), not a version.
INSTALL_HOMEBREW=0
# tmux from source (pulls libevent-dev, libncurses-dev, bison). apt otherwise.
# no-datasource: a boolean gate (build tmux from source), not a version.
TMUX_FROM_SOURCE=0
# `alias apt='nala'`. NEVER a function, and `sudo` is never redefined (K20).
# no-datasource: a boolean gate (the nala alias), not a version.
ENABLE_NALA_ALIAS=0
# pkg_upgrade only ever runs when this is 1 (or --upgrade is given).
# no-datasource: a boolean gate (run pkg_upgrade), not a version.
DEVENV_UPGRADE=0

# =============================================================================
# DELIBERATELY NOT PINNED HERE — so there are no orphan pins (MUST-FIX P3)
#
#   firecracker            no module installs it; SPEC 7.5's "module exists" is
#                          wrong, there is no such module. Documented in docs/, not
#                          installed.
#   cmctl, cert-manager /  krew `cert-manager` and `ingress-nginx` are conditional on
#   ingress-nginx          a fleet fact that this repo cannot probe from a laptop.
#                          The k9s plugins that would use them are guarded and
#                          degrade to a no-op, and docs/tools.md says so.
#   brave-browser, picom,  DELETED with modules/60-desktop.sh and profiles/desktop.list
#   mpv, tigervnc-viewer,  (SPEC-ADDENDUM C16). Terminal-only: no desktop, no
#   autocutsel, xvfb       compositor, no GUI browser in any profile. Playwright's
#                          own dep set is installed by `devenv --only headless-browser`,
#                          which delegates the list to `npx playwright install-deps`.
#   vagrant, kubeval,      dropped with reasons in SPEC 8.
#   kubent, helmfile,
#   talosctl, flux, ...
#   pipx, mise (default)   uv is the only Python installer; mise is opt-in via
#                          NODE_MANAGER=mise and needs no pin of its own beyond
#                          MISE_VERSION above.
#   pytest                 never installed globally; use `uv add --dev pytest`.
#   qrencode               apt package, installed by `auth-sso` only when
#                          DEVENV_BROWSER_QR=1. No pin needed.
#   docker-ce, terraform,  vendor apt repos decide the version. See lib/repo.sh.
#   azure-cli, gh, trivy
# =============================================================================
